<article class="env-lemma" id="00NU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00NU">Lemma <span data-tag="00NU">10.106.7</span>.</a> Suppose $R$ is a Noetherian local ring. Let $x \in \mathfrak m$ be a nonzerodivisor such that $R/xR$ is a regular local ring. Then $R$ is a regular local ring. More generally, if $x_1, \ldots , x_ r$ is a regular sequence in $R$ such that $R/(x_1, \ldots , x_ r)$ is a regular local ring, then $R$ is a regular local ring. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $x$ together with the lifts of a system of minimal generators of the maximal ideal of $R/xR$ will give $\dim (R)$ generators of $\mathfrak m$. Use Lemma <a href="/tag/00KW" data-tag="00KW">10.60.13</a>. The last statement follows from the first and induction. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>